        "Time-of-day matters significantly: slippage is lowest during US market hours (14:00–21:00 UTC) when liquidity peaks, and highest during Asian-only hours (00:00–07:00 UTC) for USD-denominated pairs. Weekend slippage can be 2–3x higher than weekday levels for the same order size and pair. These patterns are consistent across both CEXs and DEXs."
