        "For orders above $50,000: use TWAP (Time-Weighted Average Price) execution by splitting into 10+ equal parts over 1–4 hours. This approach reduces market impact and captures the average price rather than a single potentially unfavorable print. Monitor cumulative slippage across all chunks, if it exceeds the initial estimate by more than 50%, pause execution and reassess liquidity conditions."
