          `After calculating: read Required Return (10 yr) as a reality check. If it demands 60%+ annually, the plan is fragile; either lift the monthly via Monthly Needed (10 yr) or extend the deadline. Then scan the Milestone Timeline, the early bands ($100K, $500K) should arrive on a horizon you can actually stay invested through, because most plans fail by quitting, not by bad math.`
